 eries\nis one of the South Baldwin Chamber of Commerce’s premier program
 s designed to keep members informed\, engaged\, and connected to the issue
 s shaping our region. Hosted eight times each year\, these luncheons featu
 re respected\, influential speakers who bring insight on timely topics aff
 ecting our business community.\nFrom economic development and tourism to l
 ocal governance and state-level initiatives\, each program delivers releva
 nt\, real-world perspective you can take back to your business or organiza
 tion. Just as important\, the Leadership Series provides valuable opportun
 ities to build relationships with fellow professionals\, civic leaders\, a
 nd key decision-makers from across South Baldwin County.\nAgenda\n11:00 AM
 : Private Workforce & Top Investors' Meeting\n11:30 AM: Buffet Lunch cater
 ed by\nAlabama Coastal Catering\n12:00 PM: Program Begins\nInvesting in th
 e Future\nWe are proud to recognize our Education Enrichment Sponsor\,\nWa
 rren Averett\n\, for helping connect today’s students with tomorrow’s 
 opportunities.\nCommunity Spotlight — Local Nonprofit Partners\nWe are h
 onored to highlight two organizations making a meaningful impact across Ba
 ldwin County:\nUnited Way of Baldwin County\nCrosspoint Baptist Church\n\n
 ---\n🌐 View original event: https://businesshub.southbaldwinchamber.com
